      ":question/problem": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-2 \\\\ x+2y+z &=-1 \\\\ x+3y+z &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system. Select the solution $(x,y,z)$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & -5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & -5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBack substitute, starting with the last row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z &=1 \\\\ y &=-3-(1)(1) \\\\ &=-4 \\\\ x &=-2-(2)(-4) \\\\ &\\quad -(0)(1) \\\\ &=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left(6,-4,1\\right)\n$$\n\n",
