      ":question/problem": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y-z &=-2 \\\\ -x-y+2z &=5 \\\\ y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form. Select the resulting augmented matrix.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n",
